<!DOCTYPE Menu PUBLIC "-//freedesktop//DTD Menu 1.0//EN"
 "http://www.freedesktop.org/standards/menu-spec/1.0/menu.dtd">
<!--
  Installed as /etc/xdg/menus/applications.menu by configuration.nix. Nothing
  here draws a menu: the file exists so that KDE knows which applications are
  installed at all.

  kbuildsycoca6 builds the index KIO consults to answer "what opens this file",
  and it enumerates applications by walking $XDG_MENU_PREFIX + "applications.menu".
  Plasma exports that prefix and ships plasma-applications.menu; a Hyprland
  session exports nothing, so the lookup falls back to this unprefixed name, and
  with no such file installed the index came out holding zero applications.
  Dolphin then had no handler for any MIME type and met every double-click with
  an empty "Select the program you want to use" dialog, whatever mimeapps.list
  said. (The micro-2.desktop and vlc-2.desktop files that were in
  ~/.local/share/applications are leftovers from typing commands into it.)

  Three things about the shape below, all learned by watching the application
  count in ~/.cache/ksycoca6* and none of them reported as an error anywhere:

  1. Do not write a double dash inside this comment. Two of them make the XML
     malformed, the whole file is dropped, and the index silently comes out
     empty again. That is a footgun worth the sentence it takes to record.
  2. The obvious one liner, an Include of All at the top level, also yields zero
     applications. Entries only get indexed once a child Menu with its own
     Directory allocates them, hence the nesting.
  3. The file has to sit in an XDG_CONFIG_DIRS entry. $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/menus is
     not searched for the base menu, so ~/.config/menus/applications.menu does
     nothing, and this cannot be a symlink from scripts/symlinks.sh like the
     rest of the configs.

  kde-main.directory and kf5-unknown.directory come from plasma-workspace and
  are absent on benji-desktop. That only leaves the menus unnamed, which nothing
  in this setup ever draws; allocation and indexing work regardless.
-->
<Menu>
	<Name>Applications</Name>
	<Directory>kde-main.directory</Directory>
	<DefaultAppDirs/>
	<DefaultDirectoryDirs/>
	<DefaultLayout>
		<Merge type="menus"/>
		<Merge type="files"/>
	</DefaultLayout>
	<Menu>
		<Name>All</Name>
		<Directory>kf5-unknown.directory</Directory>
		<Include>
			<All/>
		</Include>
	</Menu>
</Menu>
